# 📧 SMS Spam Detector

A machine learning pipeline that classifies SMS messages as **spam** or **ham** (not spam), built with NLP preprocessing and multiple classifier benchmarks.

---

## 🧠 Model Overview

| Component | Details |
|-----------|---------|
| Dataset | SMS Spam Collection (~5,500 messages) |
| Features | TF-IDF (max 3,000 features) + MinMax scaling |
| Text preprocessing | Lowercase → Tokenize → Remove stopwords → Porter Stemmer |
| Best model | Multinomial Naive Bayes / Voting Classifier (SVM + NB + ExtraTrees) |

---

## 📊 Model Results

| Algorithm | Accuracy | Precision |
|-----------|----------|-----------|
| Naive Bayes (Multinomial) | ~97.5% | ~100% |
| Bernoulli Naive Bayes | ~97.8% | ~98.4% |
| SVM (sigmoid kernel) | ~97.1% | ~97.6% |
| Logistic Regression | ~96.8% | ~97.2% |
| Random Forest | ~97.3% | ~98.1% |
| AdaBoost | ~96.2% | ~96.0% |
| KNN | ~91.4% | ~93.0% |
| Decision Tree | ~96.4% | ~94.5% |
| **Voting Classifier (SVM+NB+ET)** | **~97.9%** | **~99.1%** |

> Precision is prioritized over accuracy — we want to minimize false positives (legitimate messages flagged as spam).

